Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: OpenGLide (qemu-xtra fork)
Upstream-Contact: KJ Liew <https://github.com/kjliew/qemu-xtra>
Source: https://github.com/kjliew/qemu-xtra
Comment: Built from qemu-xtra's openglide/ directory at the commit in packages/wsh-openglide/upstream.env
 of wsh-pve, fetched with git at build time. OpenGLide began at http://openglide.sourceforge.net;
 qemu-xtra is KJ Liew's fork of it for qemu-3dfx.

Files: *
Copyright: Fabio Barros, Paul (Glidos), Simon White and the OpenGLide contributors
           KJ Liew
License: LGPL-2.1
Comment: The source files say "OpenGLide is OpenSource under LGPL license" without a version;
 qemu-xtra's LICENSE file is the GNU LGPL version 2.1, taken here to cover the files without a
 notice of their own too.

Files: sdk2_3dfx.h sdk2_glide.h sdk2_glidesys.h sdk2_glideutl.h sdk2_sst1vid.h
Copyright: 1995, 1999 3Dfx Interactive, Inc.
License: 3dfx-Glide-GPL
Comment: The Glide 2 SDK headers (types and constants of the Glide API, compiled into the library),
 with OpenGLide's changes. 3Dfx Interactive released the Glide 2.x sources with these headers in
 1999 under the 3DFX GLIDE Source Code General Public License below (glide2x/sst1/glide/src/ and
 glide2x/sst1/init/sst1vid.h, swlibs/fxmisc/3dfx.h in https://github.com/sezero/glide). The copies
 in qemu-xtra still carry the SDK's 1995 "unpublished proprietary" banner; build.sh replaces it
 with that release's notice (packages/wsh-openglide/glide-gpl-notice.txt) and leaves the code as
 it is.

Files: gsplash.cpp gbanner.cpp splash.dat banner.dat
Copyright: 1999 3Dfx Interactive, Inc.
License: 3dfx-Glide-GPL
Comment: The Glide splash screen and banner (off by default: NoSplash, ShamelessPlug). The notice
 in these files names the 3DFX GLIDE General Public License; its text below is the glide_license.txt
 of the 3Dfx Glide source release (as kept at https://github.com/sezero/glide).

Files: fgfont.h
Copyright: 1999-2000 Pawel W. Olszta
License: X11
Comment: Bitmap fonts from FreeGLUT.

